n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"next\": \"14.2.5\",\n    \"react\": \"18.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"18.3.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.4.5\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"^20.14.0\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"^18.3.3\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^18.3.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Change #2: Next.js config\n**File:** services/frontend/next.config.js\n**Action:** Use the Write tool (new file) with the exact content below.\n**Content / new_string:**\n```\n/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\nconst nextConfig = {};\n\nmodule.exports = nextConfig;\n```\n\n### Change #3: TypeScript config (referenced by the architecture quality gate)\n**File:** services/frontend/tsconfig.json\n**Action:** Use the Write tool (new file) with the exact content below.\n**Content / new_string:**\n```\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2017\",\n    \"lib\": [\"dom\", \"dom.iterable\", \"esnext\"],\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"module\": \"esnext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"preserve\",\n    \"incremental\": true,\n    \"plugins\": [{ \"name\": \"next\" }],\n    \"paths\": { \"@/*\": [\"./*\"] }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"next-env.d.ts\", \"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\", \".next/types/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Change #4: Next TypeScript ambient declarations\n**File:** services/frontend/next-env.d.ts\n**Action:** Use the Write tool (new file) with the exact content below.\n**Content / new_string:**\n```\n/// <reference types=\"next\" />\n/// <reference types=\"next/image-types/global\" />\n\n// NOTE: This file should not be edited\n// see https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/config/typescript for more information.\n```\n\n### Change #5: Root layout (App Router requires it)\n**File:** services/frontend/app/layout.tsx\n**Action:** Use the Write tool (new file) with the exact content below.\n**Content / new_string:**\n```\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react';\n\nexport const metadata = {\n  title: 'Frontend',\n  description: 'Frontend home page',\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body>{children}</body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Change #6: Home page — the exact assertion target\n**File:** services/frontend/app/page.tsx\n**Action:** Use the Write tool (new file) with the exact content below.\nThis server component renders exactly one `<h1>` whose text is `Hello world`,\nsatisfying `expect(page.locator('h1')).toHaveText('Hello world')`.\n**Content / new_string:**\n```\nexport default function Home() {\n  return <h1>Hello world</h1>;\n}\n```\n\n### Change #7: Dockerfile — build + serve on port 3000\n**File:** services/frontend/Dockerfile\n**Action:** Use the Write tool (new file) with the exact content below.\nNotes for reliability:\n- `node:20-slim` (Debian) avoids musl/glibc edge cases.\n- Do NOT set `NODE_ENV=production` before install — that would skip\n  `typescript`/`@types`, breaking the TypeScript `next build`. `next start`\n  runs in production mode on its own.\n- `-H 0.0.0.0` (via the `start` script) binds all interfaces so the published\n  `3000:3000` mapping is reachable at `http://127.0.0.1:3000`.\n**Content / new_string:**\n```\nFROM node:20-slim\nWORKDIR /app\n\nENV NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1\n\nCOPY package.json package-lock.json* ./\nRUN npm install\n\nCOPY . .\nRUN npm run build\n\nEXPOSE 3000\nCMD [\"npm\", \"run\", \"start\"]\n```\n\n### Change #8: Docker build ignore (hygiene)\n**File:** services/frontend/.dockerignore\n**Action:** Use the Write tool (new file) with the exact content below.\n**Content / new_string:**\n```\nnode_modules\n.next\nnpm-debug.log\nDockerfile\n.dockerignore\n```\n\n## Verification Expectation\nAfter the applier writes these files, the runne